### LINK 2

**URL:** https://www.contentstack.com/docs/headless-cms/custom-preview-urls#configure-custom-preview-urls
**Posted by:** V-EPAM-Ivan Mikhailov, 2026-07-27
**Classification:** Vendor documentation (Contentstack) — **RELEVANT**
**Fetch status:** ✅ Successfully fetched

**What this document is:** A guide for configuring Custom Preview URLs in Contentstack — dynamic, pattern-based paths for Live Preview that align with website routing logic. Last updated July 22, 2026.

**This is purely configuration in the Contentstack UI — no code changes.** Quoted from the document: *"To configure Custom Preview URLs, log in to your Contentstack Account and perform the following steps: Go to your stack and click 'Settings'. Navigate to Visual Experience and select the Preview URL tab. Enable the Custom Preview URL toggle."*

**Key details (quoted):**

- Purpose: *"Custom Preview URLs allow you to define dynamic, pattern-based paths for Live Preview. These paths align preview behavior with your website's routing logic, including nested routes, taxonomies, multiple domains, and non-native URL fields."*

- Previous behavior: *"Previously, Live Preview used a fixed pattern: `<environment base URL> + <entry's native URL field>`"*

- Pattern syntax uses `{{...}}` placeholders: *"Entry fields: `{{entry.slug}}`, `{{entry.title}}`, `{{entry.uid}}`"*; *"Context variables: `{{environment}}`, `{{locale}}`, `{{branch}}`, `{{contentTypeUid}}`"*

- Configuration is per-branch and per-content-type: *"Select the Branch where the configuration applies. Choose whether the pattern applies to All content types or only to Specific content types."*

- Fallback behavior: *"Reverts to the default preview URL if resolution fails."*

- **Visual Editor integration:** *"Custom Preview URLs resolve in Visual Editor the same way they do in Live Preview. After you configure a pattern under Settings → Visual Experience → Preview URL, Visual Editor uses that configuration to resolve entry URLs on the canvas. No additional setup is required."*

- **One code-side requirement for Visual Editor:** *"To open the correct entry, the Start editing button passes the entry UID and content type UID as page context. Configure this context once in your front-end code."* — referencing `setPageContext(context)` in the Live Preview Utils SDK.

**Relevance to the story:** The ticket covers GO, UP, MX, and Interactive Maps — multiple sites with different routing structures. Custom Preview URLs are the mechanism to map Contentstack entries to the correct preview URL for each site/content type. This is relevant because the default fixed-pattern preview URL (`<base URL> + <entry's native URL field>`) likely won't work for all the different page types across GO, UP, and MX. The team would need to configure custom patterns per content type and per branch/site.

**Availability note (quoted):** *"Custom Preview URLs is available on select plans. Contact Contentstack support for more information."* — This is a potential blocker the team should verify.

